stuntcam fixture patch for Apple's sample "AVCam: Building a camera app" (zip sha256 5a1981f9...0e53; see README.md).
Apply from the top of the unzipped sample: git apply avcam.patch (or patch -p1 < avcam.patch).

Part (a), AVCam/Capture/PhotoCapture.swift: the Live Photo fix. Set the Live Photo movie URL only when Live Photo capture
  is enabled on the photo output. Without it the shutter crashes wherever Live Photo is unsupported (as under stuntcam).
Part (b), AVCam/CameraView.swift: build with Xcode 27.0. Compile the iOS 27.1-only toolbar-edge modifier only when
  AVCAM_SDK_27_1 is set; build.sh sets it when the SDK is 27.1 or later, so there the sample is unchanged. Applying by
  hand with SDK 27.1+: add AVCAM_SDK_27_1 to Active Compilation Conditions yourself.

--- a/AVCam/Capture/PhotoCapture.swift
+++ b/AVCam/Capture/PhotoCapture.swift
@@ -90,7 +90,10 @@
         photoSettings.maxPhotoDimensions = photoOutput.maxPhotoDimensions
         
         // Set the movie URL if the photo output supports Live Photo capture.
-        photoSettings.livePhotoMovieFileURL = features.isLivePhotoEnabled ? URL.movieFileURL : nil
+        // stuntcam fixture, part (a), the Live Photo fix: also require Live Photo capture to be enabled on the output.
+        // updateConfiguration enables it only where it's supported; where it isn't (stuntcam, a camera without Live Photo),
+        // a movie URL makes capturePhoto throw. Where Live Photo is supported, nothing changes.
+        photoSettings.livePhotoMovieFileURL = features.isLivePhotoEnabled && photoOutput.isLivePhotoCaptureEnabled ? URL.movieFileURL : nil
         
         // Set the priority of speed versus quality during this capture.
         if let prioritization = AVCapturePhotoOutput.QualityPrioritization(rawValue: features.qualityPrioritization.rawValue) {
--- a/AVCam/CameraView.swift
+++ b/AVCam/CameraView.swift
@@ -108,6 +108,9 @@
     CameraView(camera: PreviewCameraModel())
 }
 
+// stuntcam fixture, part (b), builds with Xcode 27.0: `toolbarVerticalEdge` is new in the iOS 27.1 SDK, so this
+// modifier is compiled only when AVCAM_SDK_27_1 is set (fixtures/avcam/build.sh sets it with SDK 27.1 or later).
+#if AVCAM_SDK_27_1
 /// A modifier that extends a view across the side where the system places the vertical toolbar.
 @available(iOS 27.1, *)
 private struct ToolbarEdgeSafeArea: ViewModifier {
@@ -127,6 +130,7 @@
         content.ignoresSafeArea(edges: edges)
     }
 }
+#endif
 
 private extension View {
 
@@ -136,11 +140,15 @@
     /// view inside the safe area.
     @ViewBuilder
     func ignoresSafeAreaAtToolbarEdge() -> some View {
+#if AVCAM_SDK_27_1
         if #available(iOS 27.1, *) {
             modifier(ToolbarEdgeSafeArea())
         } else {
             self
         }
+#else
+        self // part (b): as the sample does before iOS 27.1
+#endif
     }
 }
 
